Julia, Kevin, and Lee are painting a long straight fence. 
Julia starts with the first picket and paints every $j$th picket; 
Kevin starts with the second picket and paints every $k$th picket; 
Lee starts with the third picket and paints every $l$th picket.
Define a positive integer $100j+10k+l$ as perfectly paintable when the triple $(j,k,l)$ of positive integers results in every picket being painted exactly once by only one of the painters. Find the sum of all perfectly paintable integers.
